<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<section xml:id="course-info">
  <title>General Course Information</title>

  <introduction>
    <figure xml:id="fig-topics">
      <caption>A tour of MATH 13: space curves, surfaces, and the tangent
      planes and gradients we will use to study them.</caption>
      <image source="IMG_9751.jpeg" width="92%">
        <shortdescription>A guide welcoming you to floating islands built from the curves and surfaces studied in MATH 13</shortdescription>
        <description>
          <p>
            A colorful nighttime cartoon of a floating island landscape, each
            part built from something we study this quarter. At a stone
            gateway on the lower left, a smiling guide with a backpack and a
            walking stick extends an arm, welcoming you in. Overhead, glowing
            dotted curves arc across the sky like points tracing out paths.
            On a stone platform at the center, a purple space curve loops
            around a set of three-dimensional coordinate axes, and behind it
            stand a rainbow-colored cone, a gridded dome, and a saddle
            surface. A golden path crosses stepping stones over a stream and
            winds upward past a broad rainbow-colored hill ringed by contour
            lines and capped by a flat tangent plane, where a gold arrow
            rises from the point of tangency and blue arrows fan out across
            the plane. The path spirals on to a glowing summit at the very
            top of the landscape, while waterfalls spill off the island edges
            into the night sky. Every one of these ideas is listed in
            <xref ref="specific-goals" text="title"/>.
          </p>
        </description>
      </image>
    </figure>

    <p>
      <dl>
        <li>
          <title>Course</title>
          <p>MATH 13 <mdash/> Calculus and Analytic Geometry III</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <title>Instructor</title>
          <p>Mehdi Ahmadi. I prefer to go by my first name.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <title>Office</title>
          <p>St. Joseph's Hall 111</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <title>Email</title>
          <p><email>mahmadi@scu.edu</email></p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <title>Lecture dates</title>
          <p>
            September 21 <ndash/> December 4, 2026. The final examination period is
            December 7 <ndash/> 11, 2026.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <title>Prerequisite</title>
          <p>
            MATH 12 or equivalent. A grade of C<ndash/> or higher in MATH 12 is
            strongly recommended before taking MATH 13.
          </p>
        </li>
      </dl>
    </p>

    <p>
      This syllabus applies to both sections of MATH 13 listed in
      <xref ref="table-sections"/>. Please attend the section you are enrolled in.
    </p>

